# =====================================================================
# Trivy exceptions. Each entry: why it cannot be fixed on our side,
# why the risk is acceptable, and an expiry date to force a review.
# =====================================================================

# --- nginx:stable-alpine (latest digest, not rebuilt yet) ---
# libxml2 is fixed in Alpine (r3 to r5), but the official nginx image has not
# been rebuilt with the latest fixes yet (current digest ships r2, newest ships r3).
# libxml2 is only used by the XSLT module, which our config does not load
# (stream only, no XML parsing). CVE-2026-11979 is in the xmlcatalog CLI tool,
# never run in the container. Short expiry: upstream rebuild expected soon.
CVE-2026-86144 exp:2026-12-10
CVE-2026-11979 exp:2026-12-10
CVE-2026-86138 exp:2026-12-10
CVE-2026-86139 exp:2026-12-10
CVE-2026-86140 exp:2026-12-10
CVE-2026-86142 exp:2026-12-10
CVE-2026-86143 exp:2026-12-10

# --- certbot/certbot (5.10.0, latest release) ---
# Trivy reads a stale third-party SBOM (see Trivy warning), not what is installed.
# `pip list` in the image shows the Python environment Certbot uses is already patched:
#   - urllib3: reported 2.7.0, installed 2.8.0 (fixed)
#   - setuptools: reported 70.3.0, installed 84.2.1 (fixed)
#   - msgpack: reported 1.1.2, not installed
# Certbot is not exposed to the internet, it only runs periodically to renew certificates.

CVE-2026-114613 exp:2026-12-15
